---
import Layout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "August 20, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service | Time Reminder"
  description="Terms governing use of the free Time Reminder browser timer."
>
  <main
    id="main-content"
    class="page-shell legal-page terms-page"
    tabindex="-1"
  >
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      These Terms explain the rules for using Time Reminder, a free browser
      timer operated by justy.dev.
    </p>
    <p class="updated-note">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="agreement">
      <h2 id="agreement">1. Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing or using <strong>timeremind.info</strong> and its related pages
        (the “Service”), you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree,
        do not use the Service. Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains
        how information related to the Service is handled.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="service">
      <h2 id="service">2. The Service and Eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        Time Reminder provides audible reminders at the top, bottom, and quarter
        points of an hour. Reminder behavior depends on your browser, device,
        audio settings, and whether the page remains open. The Service is
        provided free of charge.
      </p>
      <p>
        You must be at least 13 years old to use the Service. By using it, you
        confirm that you meet this requirement and may legally use the Service
        where you are located.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="accounts">
      <h2 id="accounts">3. No Accounts</h2>
      <p>
        No account or sign-up is required. Some preferences may be stored in
        your browser using local storage. You are responsible for your device,
        browser permissions, notification and audio settings, and any loss of
        locally stored preferences caused by clearing data or changing devices.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="acceptable-use">
      <h2 id="acceptable-use">4. Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p>You may not use the Service to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Break the law, infringe rights, or facilitate harmful activity.</li>
        <li>
          Interfere with, overload, damage, or probe the Service or its
          infrastructure.
        </li>
        <li>
          Scrape, crawl, or automate access beyond ordinary browser use without
          permission.
        </li>
        <li>
          Bypass rate limits, access controls, or other technical protections.
        </li>
        <li>Distribute malware, malicious code, or abusive traffic.</li>
        <li>
          Impersonate another person or misrepresent your relationship with us.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may investigate suspected violations, limit or block access, and take
        other lawful action to protect the Service and its users.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="advertising">
      <h2 id="advertising">5. Advertising and Affiliate Links</h2>
      <p>
        The Service may display third-party advertising and include affiliate
        links, including links associated with Amazon Associates. We may earn a
        commission when you purchase through an affiliate link, at no extra cost
        to you. Advertisers and retailers control their own content,
        transactions, cookies, privacy practices, and terms. An advertisement or
        affiliate link is not a guarantee or endorsement of the linked product
        or service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="intellectual-property">
      <h2 id="intellectual-property">6. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        justy.dev and its licensors retain all rights in the Time Reminder name,
        design, code, interface, text, graphics, sounds, and other Service
        materials. We give you a limited, non-exclusive, revocable right to use
        the Service for lawful ordinary use. You may not copy, modify,
        redistribute, sell, publicly perform, or reverse engineer the Service,
        except where applicable law does not allow that restriction.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="third-parties">
      <h2 id="third-parties">7. Third-Party Services and Links</h2>
      <p>
        The Service may depend on browsers, hosting providers, analytics
